1
00:00:05,881 --> 00:00:06,882
I like her.

2
00:00:09,343 --> 00:00:12,679
I have feelings for Ms. Gong.

3
00:00:20,187 --> 00:00:21,313
You must be crazy.

4
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:23,565
What?

5
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:27,110
Mom, it's not what you think it is.

6
00:00:27,945 --> 00:00:30,155
Aunt, Nam-su, it really isn't.

7
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:33,492
Please pretend you didn't hear that.

8
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:34,868
- Look...
- Hush.

9
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:39,540
We need to talk.

10
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:51,051
What were you doing in there?

11
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:54,179
- Confessing?
- Why?

12
00:00:54,263 --> 00:00:55,889
Why else?

13
00:00:55,973 --> 00:00:58,517
- Obviously...
- Obviously, you wanted to help me.

14
00:00:58,600 --> 00:00:59,977
I know that.

15
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:02,437
But you basically

16
00:01:02,521 --> 00:01:05,232
- made a fool of me there.
- Wait, Ms. Gong.

17
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:07,901
Do you know what it means to confess
in front of my mom?

18
00:01:07,985 --> 00:01:11,321
She's going to roast me
about dating and whatnot

19
00:01:11,405 --> 00:01:13,699
my grandma's going to
call her ninth-degree relative.

20
00:01:14,032 --> 00:01:16,076
Then my grandfather will
automatically find out.

21
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:18,745
What were you thinking?

22
00:01:19,121 --> 00:01:20,831
Of all excuses,
why would you say that?

23
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:22,666
- Let me talk.
- Talk.

24
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:25,669
I agree it wasn't the best timing.

25
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:28,130
It's true I was trying to help you.

26
00:01:29,131 --> 00:01:31,008
But calling it an excuse is
quite disappointing.

27
00:01:31,091 --> 00:01:32,926
Do you think I wanted to do that?

28
00:01:34,845 --> 00:01:37,097
Mr. Dokgo, you know what?

29
00:01:37,347 --> 00:01:38,640
What I want to do is date.

30
00:01:38,724 --> 00:01:41,893
A relationship without any pressure
or interference from my family.

31
00:01:41,977 --> 00:01:44,688
A relationship about the two of us.

32
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:48,358
I wanted to know
how far my feelings could go

33
00:01:48,442 --> 00:01:50,027
when we started out physically.

34
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,278
Yeon-su.

35
00:02:06,043 --> 00:02:07,169
Father!

36
00:02:07,586 --> 00:02:08,962
- Oh, my gosh.
- What do we do?

37
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,131
What are we going to do?

38
00:02:13,050 --> 00:02:15,093
- Grandfather.
- What's all the fuss?

39
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:29,441
- Grandfather, I can explain...
- It's late.

40
00:02:29,858 --> 00:02:30,984
Get inside.

41
00:02:49,795 --> 00:02:53,715
This is why you have to watch
your mouth in the house.

42
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:55,509
They found out about my divorce

43
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:59,012
while I was fighting with his lawyer
in the backyard.

44
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,223
I wonder how much he heard.

45
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:04,059
I bet he didn't hear everything.
Right, Aunt Mi-young?

46
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:07,145
Yeon-su, haven't you heard
of the three things he was born with?

47
00:03:07,813 --> 00:03:10,440
Strong teeth, great sight, and...

48
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:12,442
- Thick hair?
- Amazing hearing.

49
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:16,488
What do I do now?

50
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:22,119
Should I beg him for forgiveness?

51
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:25,831
- I wouldn't if I were you.
- Why not?

52
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:27,666
What did you do wrong?

53
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:29,751
Sleeping with the guy you like?

54
00:03:29,835 --> 00:03:32,546
Or dating someone on your own terms?

55
00:03:35,465 --> 00:03:37,759
You might as well fight
instead of making yourself pitiful.

56
00:03:37,843 --> 00:03:40,887
The moment you beg him,
you're at fault.

57
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:44,099
I feel bad saying this to my father

58
00:03:44,182 --> 00:03:47,310
but the one who strikes first
takes control.

59
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:50,355
Let's be honest.
I didn't have anyone on my side

60
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:52,733
but you do.

61
00:03:52,816 --> 00:03:53,942
You have him.

62
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:14,713
The radish is
finally getting delicious.

63
00:04:15,589 --> 00:04:17,924
It was too dry last time.

64
00:04:18,008 --> 00:04:22,846
By the way,
why couldn't you sleep last night?

65
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:28,560
Yeon-su.

66
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:30,103
About that guy last night.

67
00:04:32,397 --> 00:04:33,482
Grandfather.

68
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:35,484
I won't make any excuses.

69
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:39,404
It's just as you saw. I...

70
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:45,660
like Mr. Dokgo Dal.

71
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:47,788
Mr. Dokgo Dal?

72
00:04:48,205 --> 00:04:49,247
Bring him home.

73
00:04:49,331 --> 00:04:52,501
But it's too early for us to think
about marriage.

74
00:04:52,584 --> 00:04:54,085
I don't want to bring him home.

75
00:04:54,169 --> 00:04:56,213
And we're not even at that point yet.

76
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:57,339
We are

77
00:04:58,548 --> 00:04:59,883
only going to date... No.

78
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:03,595
We'll start by dating.

79
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:07,140
I knew he'd do that.

80
00:05:07,891 --> 00:05:09,810
What? After...

81
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:14,439
After all that ruckus

82
00:05:14,773 --> 00:05:16,358
did he run off alone?

83
00:05:17,108 --> 00:05:18,777
- What?
- He'll obviously

84
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:21,947
take advantage of your innocent heart
and dump you.

85
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:25,116
Yet, you want to do what
with him? Dating?

86
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:27,077
Don't be stupid!

87
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:30,622
- He's not like that, Grandfather...
- If he's not, bring him home!

88
00:05:33,667 --> 00:05:34,793
Forget it.

89
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:36,753
Quit your job.

90
00:05:36,837 --> 00:05:38,380
Go on a blind date
and get married by this year.

91
00:05:42,968 --> 00:05:43,969
Answer me!

92
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,222
No, Grandfather.

93
00:05:48,515 --> 00:05:49,766
What did you just say?

94
00:05:52,227 --> 00:05:55,856
I want to stop
complying with your orders

95
00:05:56,565 --> 00:05:59,442
against my will.

96
00:06:00,068 --> 00:06:02,779
- Gong Yeon-su.
- Are you disobeying me?

97
00:06:02,863 --> 00:06:04,239
I'm not disobeying you.

98
00:06:04,948 --> 00:06:06,116
I want to be in control

99
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,410
of my own life.

100
00:06:08,994 --> 00:06:09,995
Is that so?

101
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:15,458
Then get out.

102
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:18,795
If you're going to do whatever
you want and disgrace this family

103
00:06:18,879 --> 00:06:19,880
get out.

104
00:06:22,966 --> 00:06:23,967
I said, out!

105
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:31,141
MAKE ME TINGLE

106
00:06:32,058 --> 00:06:33,935
EPISODE 9

107
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:35,478
Why did you do that, Dal?

108
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:38,857
- What do you mean?
- You're a genius strategist.

109
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,525
When we first started this business

110
00:06:40,609 --> 00:06:43,111
remember how talks and classes
were a huge hit?

111
00:06:43,194 --> 00:06:45,280
You always think several moves ahead.

112
00:06:48,491 --> 00:06:51,328
Yet that's how you ask her out?

113
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:55,832
You do realize
how things are going, right?

114
00:06:55,916 --> 00:06:56,917
I do.

115
00:06:57,167 --> 00:06:59,294
Ms. Gong is in trouble because of me

116
00:06:59,377 --> 00:07:01,588
and now that her family knows
about us

117
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:03,965
they'll start interfering.

118
00:07:04,049 --> 00:07:06,176
It's not just anyone.
It's her grandfather.

119
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:08,511
It won't just stop at interfering.

120
00:07:10,889 --> 00:07:13,808
Hey, do you think you can marry her?

121
00:07:17,646 --> 00:07:18,813
Do you realize it now?

122
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:22,901
What your impulsive confession
has put Yeon-su through?

123
00:07:24,235 --> 00:07:26,488
I know her grandfather
from playing Go with him.

124
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:29,240
He plays every move aggressively.

125
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:34,913
What if he locks her up or something
and leaves her without any water?

126
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:40,710
I'm thirsty.

127
00:07:42,963 --> 00:07:44,923
- Lock her up?
<i>- One latte, please.</i>

128
00:07:45,423 --> 00:07:46,716
Anything else you need?

129
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,593
I'm sorry

130
00:07:48,677 --> 00:07:51,846
but I work at Loand
on the fifth floor.

131
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:54,057
If you don't mind

132
00:07:54,808 --> 00:07:58,812
can you watch this
until I get off work?

133
00:07:59,479 --> 00:08:02,482
I'm sorry. We can take small bags

134
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:05,402
- but a suitcase is too big.
- Oh, it's okay then.

135
00:08:06,695 --> 00:08:07,904
Sorry about that.

136
00:08:07,988 --> 00:08:10,865
I'm sorry.
Your coffee will be ready shortly.

137
00:08:10,949 --> 00:08:11,950
Yes, thank you.

138
00:08:40,562 --> 00:08:44,190
- Did things go well last night?
- Yes, nothing happened.

139
00:08:44,482 --> 00:08:45,608
Did your grandfather...

140
00:08:45,692 --> 00:08:47,736
He didn't say anything either.

141
00:08:57,370 --> 00:09:00,165
I drank too much last night.
I'm not feeling good.

142
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:02,709
I'll head upstairs first.
Can you bring me my coffee?

143
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:04,252
Sure.

144
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:10,633
- I'm sorry I got you in trouble.
- Oh, no. Don't be.

145
00:09:11,092 --> 00:09:14,929
- Did I put you in a spot?
- No, I'm fine. Don't worry.

146
00:09:15,013 --> 00:09:17,223
- I'll meet your grandfather...
- No.

147
00:09:19,017 --> 00:09:21,519
It's between me and my family.

148
00:09:21,978 --> 00:09:26,733
So you don't need
to feel responsible.

149
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:32,238
- Here's your latte.
- Thank you.

150
00:09:32,322 --> 00:09:33,865
I'll see you upstairs.

151
00:09:34,616 --> 00:09:35,867
Okay.

152
00:09:40,038 --> 00:09:41,414
- What?
- What?

153
00:09:44,375 --> 00:09:45,543
Nothing.

154
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:58,098
Baek-hee, until I allow it

155
00:09:58,181 --> 00:09:59,557
don't let Yeon-su in.

156
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:02,102
She should've known better.

157
00:10:02,185 --> 00:10:04,104
Nam-su, you need to get a grip too.

158
00:10:04,646 --> 00:10:06,231
A woman leaves this family
after getting married

159
00:10:06,314 --> 00:10:08,149
but the honor and dignity
of this family are up to you.

160
00:10:08,691 --> 00:10:10,902
If you cross the line
like your sister

161
00:10:10,985 --> 00:10:11,986
I won't forgive you.

162
00:10:33,675 --> 00:10:34,676
Come here.

163
00:10:43,143 --> 00:10:44,269
What about cram school?

164
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:47,438
I switched to night classes.

165
00:10:47,522 --> 00:10:50,400
- What do you do during the day?
- I work during the day

166
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:54,195
and I need to take care
of Si-eun too.

167
00:10:54,279 --> 00:10:58,283
Why? Did selling the soy sauce
not get you enough money?

168
00:10:58,616 --> 00:11:01,077
I looked after those jars
for 30 years.

169
00:11:01,161 --> 00:11:02,412
Did you think I wouldn't notice?

170
00:11:07,333 --> 00:11:10,753
I need to meet her myself.

171
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:23,099
- Any news from JC?
- Yes. They offered us

172
00:11:23,183 --> 00:11:25,935
a short-term flagship location
at Hyunseong Department Store.

173
00:11:26,019 --> 00:11:28,897
If it meets the sales target, they'll
consider a long-term contract.

174
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:32,901
They left the store design
and the brand guideline up to us.

175
00:11:32,984 --> 00:11:35,278
That leaves us with the labor costs
and the initial setup cost.

176
00:11:35,361 --> 00:11:37,530
Unlike pop-ups,
there will be fixed costs.

177
00:11:37,614 --> 00:11:40,950
From what I remember,
they can offer budget support.

178
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:42,243
I'll check on that.

179
00:11:43,036 --> 00:11:45,121
Everyone, may I have your attention,
please?

180
00:11:46,414 --> 00:11:47,457
Guess what this is.

181
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:49,584
- What's that? A doll?
- No.

182
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:53,296
After six months of deliberation
and countless questions

183
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:54,964
Munch finally made
his first purchase.

184
00:11:55,048 --> 00:11:56,424
A round of applause, please.

185
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:59,844
I can't believe it.
What's gotten into him?

186
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:01,346
What did he buy?

187
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:04,933
He bought the Dreaming.
In fact, the pro version.

188
00:12:05,016 --> 00:12:09,562
- Oh, wow. He got the good one.
- It was worth giving him points.

189
00:12:09,646 --> 00:12:11,105
Inform him
about the repurchase promotion

190
00:12:11,189 --> 00:12:12,899
- and give him plenty of samples.
- Okay.

191
00:12:13,274 --> 00:12:15,777
By the way,
why did you put it in there?

192
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:18,112
- What about our own package?
- I told you last time.

193
00:12:18,196 --> 00:12:21,658
He made a special request
so his family would never catch him.

194
00:12:22,242 --> 00:12:23,284
It's a disguise.

195
00:12:24,327 --> 00:12:25,828
The rabbit looks pretty determined.

196
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:30,124
He can now just enjoy it.

197
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:32,043
I bet things will get better
between that couple.

198
00:12:54,315 --> 00:12:56,234
Did you say your name is Si-eun?

199
00:12:56,693 --> 00:12:59,404
- Yes.
- Thank you for coming.

200
00:12:59,487 --> 00:13:00,697
I know it wasn't an easy decision.

201
00:13:01,572 --> 00:13:04,242
The reason I asked
to see you today is...

202
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:05,493
May I...

203
00:13:06,661 --> 00:13:08,204
speak first?

204
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:11,874
I...

205
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:15,295
can't marry him.

206
00:13:15,378 --> 00:13:18,047
I heard you have
a 200-year-old soy sauce.

207
00:13:18,381 --> 00:13:20,508
You have 22 rituals a year

208
00:13:21,009 --> 00:13:22,385
and Nam-su is the eldest son.

209
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:26,014
I'm not confident
about focusing on raising a child...

210
00:13:28,391 --> 00:13:29,434
in a family like that.

211
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:32,562
Nam-su means a lot to me

212
00:13:33,813 --> 00:13:35,857
but I care more about my life.

213
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:48,578
Take this.

214
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:51,164
Get yourself something delicious

215
00:13:51,748 --> 00:13:53,666
and spend the rest on what you need.

216
00:13:54,709 --> 00:13:59,505
I can't interfere between you two.

217
00:14:02,216 --> 00:14:05,428
This is all I can do for you.

218
00:14:08,765 --> 00:14:09,849
I want you

219
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:15,438
to make a decision
that you can handle.

220
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:18,024
Whatever decision you make

221
00:14:18,483 --> 00:14:20,151
no one's going to blame you.

222
00:14:21,069 --> 00:14:22,362
Not even Nam-su.

223
00:14:23,905 --> 00:14:25,907
That's how I raised him.

224
00:14:33,373 --> 00:14:37,377
This is green plum syrup.
It's better than the one Nam-su took.

225
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,379
Nam-su

226
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:42,382
took after you.

227
00:14:43,841 --> 00:14:45,718
I guess that's why
he's so warmhearted.

228
00:14:59,816 --> 00:15:01,401
You need to feed her well.

229
00:15:01,484 --> 00:15:03,236
- She's so skinny.
- Mom.

230
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:09,242
I'm sorry.

231
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:11,744
Gong Nam-su.

232
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:15,206
I know you're shocked and flustered

233
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:17,166
but you're not the one
having the hardest time right now.

234
00:15:17,959 --> 00:15:20,753
So pull yourself together
and stay by her side.

235
00:15:20,837 --> 00:15:21,838
Okay?

236
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:23,798
Okay.

237
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:30,763
I'll get going now.

238
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:34,767
Bye.

239
00:15:55,872 --> 00:15:57,373
Look at our Gen Z staff.

240
00:15:57,457 --> 00:15:59,375
- Oh, wow.
- What's going on?

241
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,419
Why are you so dressed up today?

242
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:04,964
- Graduation.
- "Graduation"?

243
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:06,174
I'm clocking out.

244
00:16:06,924 --> 00:16:08,551
Mr. Dokgo, bye.

245
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:10,845
I should get going too.

246
00:16:12,722 --> 00:16:14,724
Ms. Gong, aren't you going home?

247
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:16,225
- What is that?
- Oh, well...

248
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:18,936
I still have some work left.
Go ahead.

249
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:20,730
Okay then. See you.

250
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:23,691
- Bye.
- Bye.

251
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:27,612
- Good work today.
- You too.

252
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:32,158
- Bye.
- Yeah. Bye.

253
00:16:43,085 --> 00:16:44,170
Yeah.

254
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:51,052
It's my last class with my baby wolf.

255
00:16:51,928 --> 00:16:54,764
I'll get him dolled up
and ready for graduation.

256
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:56,474
- Graduation?
- <i>Anyway, why did you call?</i>

257
00:16:56,933 --> 00:16:59,977
I wanted to ask you if you happened

258
00:17:00,061 --> 00:17:01,729
to get a call from my mom.

259
00:17:01,812 --> 00:17:03,064
No, why would she?

260
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:06,526
Actually

261
00:17:06,609 --> 00:17:08,986
- I left...
- Wait.

262
00:17:09,529 --> 00:17:10,655
Hold on.

263
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:12,657
<i>I got a call from my baby wolf.</i>
<i>Hang on.</i>

264
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:13,908
<i>Talk to you later.</i>

265
00:17:20,957 --> 00:17:22,250
<i>Do you have to do this?</i>

266
00:17:23,376 --> 00:17:27,129
If you both like each other,
at least tell your grandpa

267
00:17:27,213 --> 00:17:28,839
it's serious to put him at ease.

268
00:17:28,923 --> 00:17:30,466
Do you have to rebel like this?

269
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:33,094
But I don't want to.

270
00:17:33,177 --> 00:17:36,222
I don't want them to use my marriage
as a means to feel reassured.

271
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,599
I've been in relationships
behind your back

272
00:17:38,683 --> 00:17:40,810
and even thought about marriage.

273
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:46,274
But not because I was in love
or my feelings had grown over time.

274
00:17:46,816 --> 00:17:49,485
It was just because people said
there was a right time for marriage.

275
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:51,028
I was swept along.

276
00:17:51,821 --> 00:17:52,863
But...

277
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:58,369
I don't want to do that anymore.

278
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:00,705
At least when it comes to my marriage

279
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:05,126
I want to marry someone I truly like,
know well, and love deeply

280
00:18:05,209 --> 00:18:07,169
until those feelings build up

281
00:18:07,545 --> 00:18:11,507
to the point
where I realize it has to be him.

282
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:17,722
I understand how you feel

283
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:20,641
but it's also your duty as a child
not to upset your parents.

284
00:18:21,142 --> 00:18:23,894
And you'll never be able to persuade
your grandfather like this.

285
00:18:24,729 --> 00:18:26,105
What do you expect me to do then?

286
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:29,609
Should I go on my knees and beg?

287
00:18:29,692 --> 00:18:31,319
Just live as a girl in this family

288
00:18:31,402 --> 00:18:33,613
who's old enough to get married
instead of being myself?

289
00:18:33,904 --> 00:18:34,989
Is that how you want me to live?

290
00:18:35,615 --> 00:18:36,949
Just like you

291
00:18:37,033 --> 00:18:39,827
who lived as the Gongs'
daughter-in-law for 30 years?

292
00:18:44,457 --> 00:18:45,458
Mom.

293
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:48,419
I'm sorry

294
00:18:50,046 --> 00:18:52,006
but I'm not going to live like you.

295
00:19:08,939 --> 00:19:10,900
MOM

296
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:13,361
MOM

297
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:22,995
The minimum period is a week?

298
00:19:23,079 --> 00:19:25,247
It's more expensive than I thought.

299
00:19:25,331 --> 00:19:26,582
That's a dangerous neighborhood.

300
00:19:26,666 --> 00:19:27,958
You startled me.

301
00:19:28,042 --> 00:19:29,293
It's pretty dark there.

302
00:19:33,798 --> 00:19:36,133
Did you get kicked out of your house,
by any chance?

303
00:19:36,217 --> 00:19:39,470
No, that's not it.

304
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:41,347
It's like an act of independence.

305
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:42,431
<i>Get out!</i>

306
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:46,977
I was encouraged to live on my own

307
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:49,689
but I still walked out on my own.

308
00:19:49,772 --> 00:19:51,190
So you can say I moved out.

309
00:19:52,817 --> 00:19:54,235
I have your suitcase with me.

310
00:19:55,528 --> 00:19:57,071
What? Really?

311
00:19:59,824 --> 00:20:02,368
I drank too much last night.
I'm not feeling good.

312
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:05,162
<i>I'll head upstairs first.</i>
<i>Can you bring me my coffee?</i>

313
00:20:06,872 --> 00:20:08,332
<i>You looked like you needed some help.</i>

314
00:20:08,416 --> 00:20:10,042
So I snuck it out
and put it in my trunk.

315
00:20:12,169 --> 00:20:15,923
- Thank you so much.
- Wait here.

316
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:17,758
Mr. Yun.

317
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:22,221
Can you keep it a secret

318
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,306
from Mr. Dokgo?

319
00:20:25,307 --> 00:20:28,018
- I'll go get it.
- Thank you.

320
00:20:30,521 --> 00:20:32,273
Oh, my gosh. That's such a relief.

321
00:20:58,632 --> 00:21:00,926
- What are you doing?
- Thinking.

322
00:21:01,010 --> 00:21:02,553
About what?

323
00:21:02,636 --> 00:21:06,974
I appreciate your help,
but I don't think this is right.

324
00:21:08,893 --> 00:21:10,144
Where are you going?

325
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:11,854
That's up to me...

326
00:21:11,937 --> 00:21:14,774
What kind of guy is crazy enough
to let his girl out at this hour?

327
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:28,954
It wasn't an excuse

328
00:21:30,831 --> 00:21:32,500
when I said I liked you.

329
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:36,170
I don't have any expectations.

330
00:21:36,587 --> 00:21:38,130
Whether it's work or people

331
00:21:39,131 --> 00:21:42,927
the moment I get my hopes up
I put my heart at risk.

332
00:21:43,886 --> 00:21:47,681
But the way I protected myself
all my life...

333
00:21:49,934 --> 00:21:52,061
keeps falling apart before you.

334
00:21:53,187 --> 00:21:56,732
I want to get to know you,
and I keep getting my hopes up.

335
00:21:59,944 --> 00:22:01,237
And I get disappointed at times.

336
00:22:02,947 --> 00:22:06,700
If this is
what being in love means...

337
00:22:09,537 --> 00:22:13,040
If you're an exception...

338
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:17,711
I think it's worth taking a risk.

339
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:21,882
So what I'm saying is...

340
00:22:25,886 --> 00:22:27,471
I like you.

341
00:22:45,823 --> 00:22:48,117
You can stay upstairs.
I'll stay downstairs.

342
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:50,160
There are towels in the bathroom.

343
00:22:51,245 --> 00:22:53,205
I'll get you a new toothbrush.

344
00:22:55,374 --> 00:22:56,584
The bed...

345
00:22:58,252 --> 00:23:00,713
I don't mind sharing it with you.

346
00:23:06,093 --> 00:23:09,638
We're not just friends anymore.

347
00:23:13,601 --> 00:23:16,687
I'm a girlfriend with benefits.

348
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:22,067
There is...

349
00:23:23,611 --> 00:23:25,613
something I forgot to tell you.

350
00:23:27,156 --> 00:23:28,240
You snore.

351
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:31,535
Do you have
any hair conditioner at home?

352
00:23:31,619 --> 00:23:33,412
My hair tends to get tangled easily.

353
00:23:44,506 --> 00:23:47,051
POULTRY

354
00:23:47,134 --> 00:23:49,178
- Do you have eggs at home?
- No.

355
00:23:54,516 --> 00:23:55,851
- Laver?
- No.

356
00:23:59,939 --> 00:24:01,732
Do you have rice at least?

357
00:24:01,815 --> 00:24:03,859
What about a rice cooker?

358
00:24:06,320 --> 00:24:08,072
- Is it a little too much?
- Way too much.

359
00:24:08,364 --> 00:24:12,117
You need rice in the morning.

360
00:24:12,201 --> 00:24:14,745
At least for rice
with soy sauce and eggs.

361
00:24:15,204 --> 00:24:17,790
Only then will your brain function.

362
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:23,379
This isn't a survival camp.

363
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:25,965
It looks a lot

364
00:24:26,048 --> 00:24:28,217
but it'll be gone
after just a few meals.

365
00:24:29,385 --> 00:24:30,928
We didn't get anything for dinner.

366
00:24:35,891 --> 00:24:37,601
There's nothing for dinner here?

367
00:24:39,269 --> 00:24:40,646
Do you want dumplings?

368
00:24:50,656 --> 00:24:51,865
What time do you usually go to bed?

369
00:24:53,409 --> 00:24:55,244
- Around 1 or 2 a.m.
- What?

370
00:24:55,869 --> 00:24:56,912
Something wrong?

371
00:24:57,746 --> 00:24:59,957
I usually go to bed at 11 o'clock.

372
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:02,918
And midnight at the latest.

373
00:25:03,002 --> 00:25:04,545
Two o'clock is too late.

374
00:25:05,045 --> 00:25:06,630
I have insomnia.

375
00:25:07,172 --> 00:25:10,009
Because I sleep with the lights on.

376
00:25:19,935 --> 00:25:21,895
Why don't you give them
a call at least?

377
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:24,773
I'm sure they're all worried
about you.

378
00:25:24,857 --> 00:25:28,444
I know you are too.

379
00:25:28,527 --> 00:25:30,404
Who? Me?

380
00:25:32,614 --> 00:25:35,826
I couldn't feel more free
and comfortable right now.

381
00:25:36,285 --> 00:25:39,747
"Keep women and dishes
inside the house."

382
00:25:39,830 --> 00:25:41,874
That's what I heard growing up.

383
00:25:42,916 --> 00:25:46,378
And I was told to get married
since I got into university.

384
00:25:50,966 --> 00:25:52,176
The truth is

385
00:25:53,427 --> 00:25:54,762
I was always afraid

386
00:25:55,095 --> 00:25:59,058
that I might end up
living like a dish.

387
00:26:00,142 --> 00:26:03,771
I began marketing to protect myself.

388
00:26:04,730 --> 00:26:06,648
I thought if I looked
at the world differently

389
00:26:06,732 --> 00:26:10,444
I'd get courage to break out of it.

390
00:26:16,492 --> 00:26:17,868
The bottom line is

391
00:26:17,951 --> 00:26:21,038
this is the most unconventional thing
I've ever done in my life

392
00:26:21,121 --> 00:26:22,748
but I don't regret it.

393
00:26:24,666 --> 00:26:26,335
I won't stay here for too long.

394
00:26:26,919 --> 00:26:29,588
I'll stay at Se-ra's
and find a place of my own.

395
00:26:30,089 --> 00:26:31,090
Says who?

396
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:34,384
- What?
- Who will finish all the groceries?

397
00:26:35,094 --> 00:26:36,929
You can't leave
until you finish all that food.

398
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:40,140
Don't worry.

399
00:26:40,224 --> 00:26:41,683
It'll be gone
even before you know it.

400
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:49,024
It's good.

401
00:27:22,808 --> 00:27:24,768
Steamed rice, scallions,
eggs, and soy sauce?

402
00:27:25,144 --> 00:27:26,145
That's all?

403
00:27:26,812 --> 00:27:27,855
Sounds easy.

404
00:27:28,814 --> 00:27:30,524
The fried egg's the trick.

405
00:27:33,026 --> 00:27:34,653
Why am I studying it so hard?

406
00:27:44,872 --> 00:27:46,373
Is the butter a must?

407
00:27:54,423 --> 00:27:56,633
I came down for some water.

408
00:27:58,343 --> 00:27:59,344
I see.

409
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:48,018
So this day has finally arrived.

410
00:28:48,101 --> 00:28:50,687
It wasn't anything special,
but we had fun, right?

411
00:28:50,771 --> 00:28:52,814
It wasn't the time that was special.

412
00:28:53,899 --> 00:28:54,983
It was you.

413
00:28:58,111 --> 00:29:02,324
You really know
how to play the younger guy.

414
00:29:02,407 --> 00:29:03,951
I've enjoyed our time.

415
00:29:04,034 --> 00:29:05,702
You're officially graduated.

416
00:29:06,119 --> 00:29:07,329
Thanks.

417
00:29:07,913 --> 00:29:09,039
Thanks to you

418
00:29:09,122 --> 00:29:10,624
I'm done blaming people.

419
00:29:10,707 --> 00:29:12,668
Who were you blaming?

420
00:29:14,753 --> 00:29:18,924
Well, I hated my ex and blamed
the girls I casually dated.

421
00:29:20,342 --> 00:29:21,343
I was pretty pathetic.

422
00:29:22,094 --> 00:29:23,262
Min-hyung.

423
00:29:24,680 --> 00:29:25,847
You think

424
00:29:26,348 --> 00:29:30,185
sex is about performing flawlessly,
don't you?

425
00:29:30,978 --> 00:29:33,146
But as you read
your partner's signals

426
00:29:33,230 --> 00:29:36,191
communicate, and share that intimacy

427
00:29:37,109 --> 00:29:40,404
you discover as much about yourself
as you do about the other person.

428
00:29:40,988 --> 00:29:43,907
You find out what you like

429
00:29:44,700 --> 00:29:47,619
and how you connect.

430
00:29:49,746 --> 00:29:53,625
You lacked confidence only because

431
00:29:54,376 --> 00:29:56,545
you didn't know yourself.

432
00:29:59,464 --> 00:30:01,091
I did nothing.

433
00:30:01,425 --> 00:30:02,843
You figured it out.

434
00:30:12,978 --> 00:30:14,104
<i>The call cannot be connected...</i>

435
00:30:17,065 --> 00:30:18,233
<i>The call cannot...</i>

436
00:30:18,317 --> 00:30:20,694
<i>Si-eun, you're not home,</i>
<i>and you won't answer your phone.</i>

437
00:30:20,986 --> 00:30:22,112
<i>Where on earth are you?</i>

438
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:24,197
<i>Please pick up.</i>

439
00:30:24,823 --> 00:30:26,533
<i>We promised</i>
<i>to discuss everything together.</i>

440
00:31:00,692 --> 00:31:01,943
Hello?

441
00:31:05,697 --> 00:31:09,326
Is Grandpa furious?

442
00:31:10,327 --> 00:31:12,829
<i>What about Mom?</i>

443
00:31:12,913 --> 00:31:16,792
Your mom? She hasn't batted an eye.

444
00:31:16,875 --> 00:31:18,418
She's as rigid as ever.

445
00:31:19,795 --> 00:31:22,089
<i>So stop worrying</i>
<i>about things on this end.</i>

446
00:31:22,589 --> 00:31:26,301
<i>- Focus on your getaway for now.</i>
- Okay.

447
00:31:27,260 --> 00:31:28,804
I'll call you back, Aunt.

448
00:31:29,763 --> 00:31:30,931
Bye.

449
00:31:56,248 --> 00:31:57,833
CONTACTS
MOM

450
00:32:00,293 --> 00:32:02,170
CONTACTS
MOM

451
00:32:53,513 --> 00:32:55,098
<i>Something came up,</i>
<i>and I'm heading out first.</i>

452
00:32:55,182 --> 00:32:56,475
<i>Make sure you eat.</i>

453
00:33:01,354 --> 00:33:04,399
Seriously? How cute.

454
00:33:07,235 --> 00:33:08,528
Looks good.

455
00:33:18,788 --> 00:33:19,831
Salty!

456
00:33:35,388 --> 00:33:37,140
My fortune foretold

457
00:33:38,058 --> 00:33:39,059
a disaster in my later years.

458
00:33:40,143 --> 00:33:42,604
I believe you're that very disaster.

459
00:33:43,605 --> 00:33:46,316
Perhaps, it referred
to wealth rather than disaster.

460
00:33:46,399 --> 00:33:49,319
My fortune is rich in metal,
so wealth naturally follows.

461
00:33:49,402 --> 00:33:50,820
Wealth is meaningless without virtue.

462
00:33:50,904 --> 00:33:54,032
A man must take care of himself
and his family.

463
00:33:54,115 --> 00:33:56,785
And a gentleman must uphold loyalty.

464
00:33:56,868 --> 00:33:59,454
If you don't know your basic duties,
how can you call yourself a man?

465
00:34:06,211 --> 00:34:08,296
If a man stays true to his roots
and remains consistent

466
00:34:08,380 --> 00:34:12,884
water can eventually pierce the stone
and sincerity will move the heavens.

467
00:34:13,843 --> 00:34:16,304
Surely, the heavens
will recognize my true intentions.

468
00:34:18,682 --> 00:34:20,642
Enough of that.
Why are you really here?

469
00:34:20,725 --> 00:34:23,103
I'm here to put
Ms. Gong's mind at ease.

470
00:34:23,186 --> 00:34:25,188
Why would you do that here?

471
00:34:25,272 --> 00:34:26,356
She left the house.

472
00:34:27,774 --> 00:34:30,151
Because her heart remains
in this house.

473
00:34:30,235 --> 00:34:31,444
What?

474
00:34:31,528 --> 00:34:34,322
Honestly, your permission isn't
an absolute requirement for me.

475
00:34:34,906 --> 00:34:38,285
My own feelings matter more to me
even if you don't like me.

476
00:34:38,368 --> 00:34:40,036
But Ms. Gong is different.

477
00:34:40,954 --> 00:34:42,205
She can truly be happy with me

478
00:34:42,289 --> 00:34:45,292
only if she has
her family's blessing.

479
00:34:47,627 --> 00:34:51,214
Please give us
your permission to date.

480
00:34:55,927 --> 00:35:00,140
So you're digging into my patience
just to put her mind at ease?

481
00:35:00,223 --> 00:35:01,975
With all due respect

482
00:35:02,601 --> 00:35:05,520
you sometimes have to stir the pot
to see what's inside.

483
00:35:05,895 --> 00:35:07,063
Such as

484
00:35:08,481 --> 00:35:10,817
how much you love your granddaughter.

485
00:35:13,445 --> 00:35:15,864
I don't like you.

486
00:35:16,489 --> 00:35:18,450
Since my permission
means so little to you anyway

487
00:35:18,533 --> 00:35:19,909
you don't mind me saying this, right?

488
00:35:21,536 --> 00:35:24,873
Could I ask what it is
that you hate about me?

489
00:35:25,373 --> 00:35:27,208
First, your cowardly attitude

490
00:35:27,292 --> 00:35:30,295
in masking irresponsibility
as prudence.

491
00:35:31,004 --> 00:35:33,006
Second, you're way too tall.

492
00:35:33,673 --> 00:35:34,966
And crucially, third.

493
00:35:37,761 --> 00:35:39,471
You shoot blanks.

494
00:35:39,721 --> 00:35:41,348
Wait, blanks?

495
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:43,975
I'm azoospermic.

496
00:35:44,059 --> 00:35:46,978
So I probably won't ever have
children of my own.

497
00:35:47,312 --> 00:35:48,938
- Oh, that...
- Now, leave.

498
00:35:49,648 --> 00:35:51,608
- Sir.
- Mi-young.

499
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:53,276
See the guest out.

500
00:35:55,403 --> 00:35:57,697
No hard feelings.

501
00:35:58,323 --> 00:35:59,324
You know that, right?

502
00:36:04,621 --> 00:36:06,414
Sprinkle a lot!

503
00:36:09,626 --> 00:36:10,669
Sorry.

504
00:36:17,384 --> 00:36:18,760
This is certainly not easy.

505
00:36:24,849 --> 00:36:25,975
Wait.

506
00:36:29,729 --> 00:36:32,232
Can we talk for a second?

507
00:36:34,859 --> 00:36:37,821
Yeon-su left the house.

508
00:36:39,864 --> 00:36:40,865
You know that, right?

509
00:36:43,451 --> 00:36:45,078
Do you have any idea where she is?

510
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:51,376
She said she was crashing
at a close friend's place.

511
00:36:57,716 --> 00:36:58,967
It's my fault.

512
00:37:00,260 --> 00:37:02,512
I was so caught up being
a daughter-in-law of this family

513
00:37:03,054 --> 00:37:06,015
that I failed
to look into my own child's feelings.

514
00:37:07,475 --> 00:37:09,060
She kept everything bottled up

515
00:37:09,144 --> 00:37:10,812
without a single complaint
her entire life.

516
00:37:11,896 --> 00:37:14,274
And now, it's finally blown up.

517
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:21,489
It shows how strong she is
to have endured all that time.

518
00:37:24,075 --> 00:37:25,952
She's wise.

519
00:37:26,369 --> 00:37:28,455
She knows how to make

520
00:37:29,164 --> 00:37:31,207
the right choices for herself.

521
00:37:34,335 --> 00:37:35,712
So you didn't

522
00:37:36,421 --> 00:37:37,756
fail her.

523
00:37:39,090 --> 00:37:40,550
You were simply
protecting your family.

524
00:37:46,431 --> 00:37:50,435
Tell me. Can I place my trust in you?

525
00:37:50,769 --> 00:37:53,271
Please put your faith
in your daughter's decision.

526
00:37:57,484 --> 00:37:59,736
He went to that house again?
At that hour of the morning?

527
00:37:59,819 --> 00:38:01,905
<i>It's clearly not casual between them.</i>

528
00:38:01,988 --> 00:38:02,989
<i>But the vibe is just off.</i>

529
00:38:03,072 --> 00:38:04,115
What do you mean?

530
00:38:04,199 --> 00:38:08,745
<i>Word is, the elder of the household</i>
<i>is quite displeased with your son.</i>

531
00:38:08,828 --> 00:38:11,581
- What's wrong with my boy?
<i>- Beats me.</i>

532
00:38:12,123 --> 00:38:14,751
<i>You really should</i>
<i>ask him directly now.</i>

533
00:38:14,834 --> 00:38:16,753
He'd have to actually
answer my calls for...

534
00:38:17,504 --> 00:38:19,506
Anyway, I understand.
I'll be in touch.

535
00:38:23,885 --> 00:38:24,969
Let's head to his office.

536
00:38:26,346 --> 00:38:28,223
No, wait. Take me to his house.

537
00:38:28,807 --> 00:38:29,849
Yes, sir.

538
00:38:31,434 --> 00:38:35,522
<i>- The scallions are a bit...</i>
<i>- They'll cook in the leftover heat.</i>

539
00:39:12,058 --> 00:39:13,476
Lots of sesame seeds.

540
00:39:30,785 --> 00:39:31,911
DOKGO DAL

541
00:39:35,164 --> 00:39:36,499
Where have you been all this...

542
00:39:51,180 --> 00:39:53,933
- Are you two living together?
- No, absolutely not.

543
00:39:54,142 --> 00:39:55,768
I mean, I admit

544
00:39:55,852 --> 00:39:58,813
this situation leaves plenty of room
for misunderstanding.

545
00:39:59,480 --> 00:40:01,316
But it's nothing of the sort.

546
00:40:01,399 --> 00:40:04,652
I'm just crashing here temporarily
for personal reasons.

547
00:40:04,736 --> 00:40:05,737
So you're living together.

548
00:40:10,283 --> 00:40:12,744
Have you eaten yet?

549
00:40:14,412 --> 00:40:16,706
If you like <i>cheonggukjang...</i>

550
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:20,126
Look here.

551
00:40:20,585 --> 00:40:22,587
Do I look like I have the time
to come here just to eat?

552
00:40:25,632 --> 00:40:27,634
It tastes like
what my grandma used to make.

553
00:40:33,640 --> 00:40:35,266
Is it to your liking?

554
00:40:35,350 --> 00:40:36,351
It's so good.

555
00:40:45,652 --> 00:40:47,153
Is your family aware
that you're staying here?

556
00:40:48,237 --> 00:40:50,615
No, they have no idea.

557
00:40:51,616 --> 00:40:52,867
Are you going to marry Dal?

558
00:40:55,244 --> 00:40:57,956
We haven't reached that stage yet.

559
00:40:58,039 --> 00:41:00,500
What need is there for stages?
You just proceed with it.

560
00:41:00,583 --> 00:41:03,586
Marriage is one
of life's greatest milestones.

561
00:41:03,670 --> 00:41:06,464
It's hardly something one can
easily repeat twice or thrice.

562
00:41:11,135 --> 00:41:12,136
Not that it is

563
00:41:12,679 --> 00:41:14,597
strictly forbidden, of course.

564
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:20,478
But personally,
I think one time is enough.

565
00:41:24,983 --> 00:41:25,984
I apologize.

566
00:41:27,610 --> 00:41:30,238
- Let me ask you a favor.
- Please go ahead.

567
00:41:30,738 --> 00:41:32,240
Make him shut down

568
00:41:32,740 --> 00:41:33,825
his current business.

569
00:41:34,909 --> 00:41:37,495
- Pardon?
- You two seem pretty serious.

570
00:41:37,704 --> 00:41:39,497
If marriage is
eventually on the table

571
00:41:39,789 --> 00:41:41,124
shutting that business
is the right course.

572
00:41:42,083 --> 00:41:44,127
He's capable and intelligent.

573
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:46,462
Don't you also think

574
00:41:46,546 --> 00:41:47,839
what he's doing is
a waste of his intellect?

575
00:41:51,968 --> 00:41:56,723
Sir, you trust
your son's capabilities

576
00:41:57,598 --> 00:42:00,143
yet you don't trust his judgment?

577
00:42:00,685 --> 00:42:03,312
You openly acknowledge his talent.

578
00:42:04,022 --> 00:42:08,735
Shouldn't you trust the decisions
he makes with that very talent?

579
00:42:49,025 --> 00:42:52,070
The one lounging at home
should be doing this.

580
00:42:52,153 --> 00:42:55,031
Why must I be out
doing this at this hour?

581
00:42:56,783 --> 00:42:58,326
Regardless of who comes or goes

582
00:42:58,743 --> 00:43:01,454
all he does is
lie around and sleep all day.

583
00:43:09,796 --> 00:43:11,255
Jeez.

584
00:43:18,054 --> 00:43:19,305
Why is this...

585
00:43:20,181 --> 00:43:23,601
After six months of deliberation
and countless questions

586
00:43:23,684 --> 00:43:24,894
Munch finally made
his first purchase.

587
00:43:24,977 --> 00:43:28,856
<i>He made a special request</i>
<i>so his family would never catch him.</i>

588
00:43:28,940 --> 00:43:30,024
<i>It's a disguise.</i>

589
00:43:32,360 --> 00:43:33,945
I'M IN A SEXLESS MARRIAGE
WILL THIS HELP US?

590
00:43:34,028 --> 00:43:35,446
PLEASE MAKE SURE
WITH THE DECOY PACKAGING

591
00:43:35,530 --> 00:43:36,781
He's Munch?

592
00:43:45,164 --> 00:43:46,165
You're back.

593
00:43:56,342 --> 00:43:58,594
Where have you been all day?

594
00:43:58,678 --> 00:43:59,679
You didn't call.

595
00:44:01,764 --> 00:44:04,600
I had to meet someone.
I swung by the factory too.

596
00:44:04,684 --> 00:44:05,685
Who?

597
00:44:08,229 --> 00:44:09,730
I mean, you could've told me

598
00:44:09,814 --> 00:44:12,859
when you were coming back
or if you were dining out.

599
00:44:12,942 --> 00:44:16,195
It'd be considerate to inform
the person waiting at home.

600
00:44:19,866 --> 00:44:22,702
- You waited a lot for me.
- I made enough stew for two

601
00:44:22,785 --> 00:44:24,537
but the other person wasn't here.

602
00:44:26,914 --> 00:44:30,084
Actually, I went to see
Grandfather today.

603
00:44:30,168 --> 00:44:33,045
Oh, you have a grandfather too?

604
00:44:36,007 --> 00:44:37,717
Wait. No way.

605
00:44:38,676 --> 00:44:39,844
Why on earth?

606
00:44:39,927 --> 00:44:42,805
I left that house so you wouldn't
have to deal with my family.

607
00:44:42,889 --> 00:44:44,682
Why did you go there
without telling me?

608
00:44:47,018 --> 00:44:49,145
I'm getting scolded all day today.

609
00:44:52,231 --> 00:44:54,275
Did you get told off a lot?

610
00:45:00,531 --> 00:45:04,452
I finally get why
you could never stand up

611
00:45:05,620 --> 00:45:06,787
to your grandfather.

612
00:45:07,163 --> 00:45:09,540
Why else would I have gone
so far as to leave the house?

613
00:45:21,719 --> 00:45:24,555
- What?
- I'm just proud of you.

614
00:45:28,517 --> 00:45:29,769
Should we have dinner?

615
00:45:29,852 --> 00:45:31,437
You said you made <i>cheonggukjang.</i>

616
00:45:31,771 --> 00:45:34,232
Oh, that's all gone.

617
00:45:34,315 --> 00:45:36,025
You ate two servings alone?

618
00:45:36,692 --> 00:45:39,070
- No, with your father.
- What?

619
00:45:41,614 --> 00:45:42,740
Are you serious?

620
00:45:43,366 --> 00:45:46,702
- He dropped by out of nowhere.
- And you didn't even tell me?

621
00:45:47,411 --> 00:45:49,789
What was I supposed to do?
He barged right in.

622
00:45:49,872 --> 00:45:53,709
He said he hadn't eaten,
and the <i>cheonggukjang </i>was ready.

623
00:45:54,460 --> 00:45:56,254
What did he say this time?

624
00:45:56,337 --> 00:45:57,505
Why did he come?

625
00:45:59,507 --> 00:46:00,758
Out of concern?

626
00:46:01,968 --> 00:46:04,470
Out of love for his son?

627
00:46:07,056 --> 00:46:08,849
Don't be so hard on your father.

628
00:46:09,183 --> 00:46:10,851
He may be clumsy
at expressing himself

629
00:46:10,935 --> 00:46:13,271
but no parent is clumsy
in their love for their child.

630
00:46:13,354 --> 00:46:16,941
Then, you should go back
and make up with your grandfather.

631
00:46:17,024 --> 00:46:19,360
Since he is merely clumsy
in his expression too.

632
00:46:19,694 --> 00:46:21,821
My grandpa isn't clumsy.

633
00:46:21,904 --> 00:46:23,489
His ways are set in stone.

634
00:46:23,572 --> 00:46:25,032
There's a huge 30-year gap

635
00:46:25,116 --> 00:46:27,118
between being in your 50s
and your 80s.

636
00:46:27,827 --> 00:46:30,454
Time and age don't matter
when it comes to how a parent feels

637
00:46:30,538 --> 00:46:32,039
about their child.

638
00:46:32,123 --> 00:46:33,332
Isn't that right?

639
00:46:33,708 --> 00:46:35,167
I'm heading up.

640
00:46:39,922 --> 00:46:41,299
Stay a bit longer.

641
00:46:42,008 --> 00:46:43,009
I'm bored.

642
00:47:02,695 --> 00:47:03,696
MOM

643
00:47:03,779 --> 00:47:04,780
Answer it.

644
00:47:07,825 --> 00:47:11,037
- I don't want to.
- She'll be worried. Pick up already.

645
00:47:16,125 --> 00:47:18,711
- I'll head upstairs.
- Okay.

646
00:47:43,694 --> 00:47:44,695
Are you asleep?

647
00:47:47,948 --> 00:47:49,200
Not yet.

648
00:47:50,284 --> 00:47:51,827
Is the lighting keeping you up?

649
00:48:32,868 --> 00:48:35,121
I'm sorry. I can't stand this.

650
00:48:41,127 --> 00:48:42,211
Jeez, you scared me.

651
00:48:44,713 --> 00:48:45,881
Let's stay together.

652
00:48:53,347 --> 00:48:54,849
I'll stay with you.

653
00:51:48,772 --> 00:51:50,399
DO NOT COMPARE YOURSELF TO OTHERS

654
00:51:51,233 --> 00:51:52,985
IF I GET LOST, SO DOES THE BRAND!

655
00:51:54,945 --> 00:51:56,447
JUST BE YOU

656
00:52:15,174 --> 00:52:17,843
Let's sleep upstairs together
starting tomorrow.

657
00:52:18,844 --> 00:52:20,679
The couch is fine

658
00:52:21,930 --> 00:52:23,182
but it's a bit cramped.

659
00:52:30,064 --> 00:52:31,065
Sounds good.

660
00:52:35,778 --> 00:52:37,321
Who could be visiting at this hour?

661
00:52:40,115 --> 00:52:43,577
- Could it be Mr. Yun?
- No, that's highly unlikely.

662
00:52:47,581 --> 00:52:48,749
Se-ra?

663
00:52:49,291 --> 00:52:51,710
Wait. Why is she here?

664
00:52:52,002 --> 00:52:54,046
- How...
- You mean, SR's CEO?

665
00:52:55,631 --> 00:52:56,715
I seriously have no idea.

666
00:52:58,467 --> 00:53:00,469
Why would she be here?

667
00:53:05,849 --> 00:53:07,893
Se-ra, what brings you here?

668
00:53:25,160 --> 00:53:26,370
Mom...

669
00:53:35,087 --> 00:53:38,215
MAKE ME TINGLE

670
00:55:12,267 --> 00:55:14,228
Subtitles by Songmi You
and Eunjin Erica Kim
